Error [jet.NonCAbiType]: `Point` is not a C-compatible type for a foreign function parameter or return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3203_struct_needs_layout_c.jet:7:39
    |
  7 |     make_point: fn(x: Int, y: Int) -> Point = "demo_make_point"
    |                                       ^^^^^
 Why: `#Import` / `#Export` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge.
 Fix: Use scalars, `String`, or a struct with C layout; pointers only through the gated tier.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3203
